    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: # Modern Guestbook
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: A modern, feature-rich guestbook application built with PHP, JavaScript, and MySQL.
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: ## Features
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: - Clean, responsive design
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: - Real-time message updates
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: - Rich text formatting with BBCode support
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: - Emoji support
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: - File attachments
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: - Anti-spam protection
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: - Message scheduling
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: - Search functionality
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: - Visitor statistics
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: ## Prerequisites
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: - PHP 7.4 or higher
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: - MySQL 5.7 or higher
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: - Web server (Apache/Nginx)
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: - Modern web browser
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: ## Installation
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: 1. Clone the repository:
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: 2. Create a MySQL database and import the schema:
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: 3. Configure the database connection:
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: - Copy `config.php.example` to `config.php`
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: - Update the database credentials in `config.php`
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: 4. Set up your web server:
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: - Point your web server to the project's root directory
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: - Ensure the `uploads` directory is writable by the web server
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: ## Configuration
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: - Rate limiting: Adjust timing in `php/save_entry.php`
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: - Entries per page: Modify `$per_page` in `php/get_entries.php`
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: - Maximum upload size: Configure in your PHP settings
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: - WebSocket server: Update URL in `js/main.js`
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: ## Usage
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: 1. Access the guestbook through your web browser
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: 2. Fill out the form with your name, email, and message
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: 3. Use the formatting toolbar to style your message
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: 4. Submit your entry
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: ## Security Features
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: - XSS protection
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: - CSRF protection
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: - Rate limiting
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: - Input validation
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: - Prepared SQL statements
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: ## Contributing
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: 1. Fork the repository
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: 2. Create your feature branch (`git checkout -b feature/AmazingFeature`)
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: 3. Commit your changes (`git commit -m 'Add some AmazingFeature'`)
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: 4. Push to the branch (`git push origin feature/AmazingFeature`)
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: 5. Open a Pull Request
